                        "glosses": [
                            "Any brown alga of the genus Dictyota."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d5814553-3091-49bc-ab9d-7c92aadbfcbc",
                                "sense_id": "f903e5b7-67b0-3b8f-82a2-b3d8b8f5df45",
                                "text": "Dictyota liturata J. Ag. and Dictyota Pappeana Kütz., as figured in Kutzing, Tab. Phyc., Vol. IX, Pl. 38, resemble in habit two extreme forms of this species, but both of them, as well as Dictyota Binghamiana, appear to be true Dictyotas, the internal layer never haying more than one series of cells."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e2aee0f-250d-441d-96a5-0b0755b82177",
                                "sense_id": "f903e5b7-67b0-3b8f-82a2-b3d8b8f5df45",
                                "text": "I think many dictyotas can be a hassle. The stuff I had broke apart easily and any fragments would attach and grow wherever they landed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2514252d-93fc-4555-b74a-bc85aa7b292a",
                                "sense_id": "f903e5b7-67b0-3b8f-82a2-b3d8b8f5df45",
                                "text": "The dictyota I had that was invasive was a silvery color."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
